# Milestone: M5
# Covers: D-event-1 determinism rule (spec #3 §10.2): N subscribers on the
#         same event receive emission in registration order; M successive emits
#         maintain that order across all M firings.  Run under all 3 tunable
#         presets × 100 runs each to assert byte-identical output.
#
# blocked: needs a `## host:` body.  The host driver has existed since
# the core re-foundation (tests/integration/chk_host_driver.c) -- what is
# missing is this fixture, rewritten to drive its own clock and its own
# urbi_step calls.  That is per-fixture authoring work, scheduled with the
# rest of the corpus in Phase 5.  The annotation it replaced said the
# driver did not exist, which stopped being true at Task 12.
# matrix-row: reactive-event
#
# Reason:
#   The language half is live: Event.new(), `at (e?)`, `e!(1)` and the
#   registration-order walk are covered by reactive/event/event_multi_sub_fifo.chk.
#   What is missing is the RUNNER feature this fixture exists for -- running one
#   source under every tunable preset, many times, and asserting byte-identical
#   output.  There is no `## tunables: presets` directive to write.
#
# Activate when the runner grows multi-preset mode.
#
# Urbiscript source:
#   var e = Event.new();
#   var seq = "";
#   at (e?) function (p) { seq = seq + "A" + p };
#   at (e?) function (p) { seq = seq + "B" + p };
#   at (e?) function (p) { seq = seq + "C" + p };
#   e!(1); e!(2); e!(3);
#   echo(seq);
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "A1B1C1A2B2C2A3B3C3"
